WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.468 align:start size:94% position:6%
-After the first
presidential debate,

00:00:01.468 --> 00:00:02.769 align:start size:94% position:6%
many Americans were left
with mixed feelings.

00:00:02.769 --> 00:00:05.705
Here to talk about it is one
of our writers, Jeff Wright,

00:00:05.705 --> 00:00:08.408 align:start size:94% position:6%
in a segment called
"The Wright Thing."

00:00:08.408 --> 00:00:12.812 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:00:12.812 --> 00:00:13.713 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-What it do, Seth?

00:00:13.713 --> 00:00:15.315 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hey, Jeff,
so, what did you think

00:00:15.315 --> 00:00:16.683 align:start size:94% position:6%
about the first
presidential debate?

00:00:16.683 --> 00:00:19.719 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think the Black community
is owed an apology.

00:00:19.719 --> 00:00:21.855 align:start size:94% position:6%
-From President Trump?
-Nah.

00:00:21.855 --> 00:00:23.623 align:start size:94% position:6%
-From Joe Biden?
-Nope.

00:00:23.623 --> 00:00:27.060 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Then from who?
-From America, Seth.

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:28.228 line:92%
-Why do you feel that Americ

00:00:28.228 --> 00:00:30.563 align:start size:94% position:6%
owes the Black community
an apology?

00:00:30.563 --> 00:00:32.365 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Several reasons.
Mainly slavery.

00:00:32.365 --> 00:00:35.869 align:start size:94% position:6%
But America needs to apologize
for its lies.

00:00:35.869 --> 00:00:36.970 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Lies?
-Yes, Seth, lies.

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:40.540
For several years, everyone made
it seem like only Black people

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:43.843 align:start size:94% position:6%
were ratchet and loud,
but it turns out those title

00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:46.446 align:start size:94% position:6%
should be reserved
for the presidential debate.

00:00:46.446 --> 00:00:47.547 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, because of
all the interrupting.

00:00:47.547 --> 00:00:50.583
-Yeah, I didn't know if I wa
watching the presidential debate

00:00:50.583 --> 00:00:52.419 align:start size:94% position:6%
or "The Real Housewives
of Atlanta."

00:00:52.419 --> 00:00:53.553 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, I love that show.
-Me too!

00:00:53.553 --> 00:00:57.123 align:start size:94% position:6%
Especially when -- Remembe
when Porsha got into it with -

00:00:57.123 --> 00:00:57.690 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Never mind, Seth.

00:00:57.690 --> 00:01:00.927 align:start size:94% position:6%
Point is, the Black communit
is owed an apology.

00:01:00.927 --> 00:01:02.962 size:88% position:44%
-But what did you think
about the debate itself?

00:01:02.962 --> 00:01:06.699 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I thought it was familiar
Like, in a scary way.

00:01:06.699 --> 00:01:07.534 size:81% position:41% line:92%
Because it reminded me

00:01:07.534 --> 00:01:09.269 align:start size:94% position:6%
of my brothers arguing
in front of my mom.

00:01:09.269 --> 00:01:12.305
I was just waiting for a sanda
to come flying out of nowhere.

00:01:12.305 --> 00:01:14.574
Especially when Biden told Trump
to shut up,

00:01:14.574 --> 00:01:15.775 line:92%
even my dog's ears perked up

00:01:15.775 --> 00:01:17.243 align:start size:94% position:6%
He was like,
"Who you talking to, Jeff?

00:01:17.243 --> 00:01:18.845 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like,
"Not you, Clifford.

00:01:18.845 --> 00:01:20.246 size:78% position:39% line:92%
It's okay. Good boy."

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:21.347 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-Oh, your dog can talk?

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:23.917 align:start size:94% position:6%
-All dogs can, Seth.
If they like you enough.

00:01:23.917 --> 00:01:27.654
Now, many Americans may have
been taken aback by the debate

00:01:27.654 --> 00:01:29.089 size:84% position:42% line:92%
but not the Black ones.

00:01:29.089 --> 00:01:30.590 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, no?
-Not at all.

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:31.558 size:84% position:42% line:92%
That debate looked like

00:01:31.558 --> 00:01:32.959 align:start size:94% position:6%
a regular Wednesday
at a barbershop.

00:01:32.959 --> 00:01:36.162
It had everything you could find
at your local barbershop.

00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:39.032 align:start size:94% position:6%
Two men
in desperate need of a haircut

00:01:39.032 --> 00:01:40.166 line:92%
and another sitting in the chair

00:01:40.166 --> 00:01:42.435 align:start size:94% position:6%
telling everyone
it's the other guy's turn.

00:01:42.435 --> 00:01:44.838 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, so that's what goes o
at a barbershop?

00:01:44.838 --> 00:01:47.507
-Yeah.
They don't do that at Supercuts?

00:01:47.507 --> 00:01:49.642 line:92%
-I don't go to Supercuts.

00:01:49.642 --> 00:01:50.877 line:92%
Plus you said that you would

00:01:50.877 --> 00:01:52.779 align:start size:94% position:6%
take me to a barbershop
with you.

00:01:52.779 --> 00:01:55.915 line:92%
-I said that? I did say that

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:57.951 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know what?
But you have a show to do.

00:01:57.951 --> 00:01:59.152 line:92%
We can go after your show.

00:01:59.152 --> 00:02:01.888 size:75% position:38%
-Yeah, you said that
the last time, Jeff.

00:02:01.888 --> 00:02:04.557 line:92%
-I said that? I did say that

00:02:04.557 --> 00:02:06.793 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know what?
I mean it this time, Seth.

00:02:06.793 --> 00:02:08.895 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You said that
the last time, too.

00:02:08.895 --> 00:02:10.363 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I said that?

00:02:10.363 --> 00:02:12.599 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:02:12.599 --> 00:02:15.869 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"The Wright Thing"
with Jeff Wright, everybody.

